Z||000015||olympic||06-27-2000||08:29 PM||||Formula,<BR>   There was a study done years ago that tried to find a common thread or belief common to all Canadians.  It was a pretty difficult task since Canadians believe in a mosaic cultural system where people retain their own individual culture and beliefs as opposed to the american "melting pot" culture .  The only common thread they could find was that every Canadian strongly believes that they are NOT "Americans".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Our system of government and our history is quite dissimilar from the USA's which makes us feel distinctly different from the US.  Call us crazy canucks but you wont see many of us rushing to join the good ol US of A if the offer was made.<P>   Here's something I've been wondering about for years.  Somebody told me that if you ask an american what nationality they are, more than likely he/she will answer "I'm an american!"  Ask a Canadian the same question and none will say "I'm a Canadian!"(except those wierdo's in the Molson comercials  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )  They will say German, Ukranian, French, etc.  Is this true or just another stereotype??||||reg||1
