Z||000026||BN Boomer||06-30-2000||03:48 PM||||Canada sucks! Well sort of. Why is that any Canadian citizen can come down to the US to work but for one of us to go up there to work we either need a work visa or dual citizenship? I could go up to Vancouver, BC and make some big bucks working on a temporary transfer with the railroad I am employed by if I could meet either of those requirements. I'm surprised they even let us Yanks operate our own trains as far into Canada as Vancouver. The RTC is a pain in the arse, too. Sorry, but you guys are way too overregulated.<P>Personally, I think we should just annex Western Canada. That would probably even make those French goofballs in Quebec happy.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Here's another question for our Bretheren of the North, can you still buy the smaller cans of R12 freon refrigerant up there?||||reg||1
Z||000027||DaRkLoRD||06-30-2000||05:00 PM||||Yeah, Canada is WAAY too over-regulated.. not to mention over-taxed.. but that's a different story.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>JohnnyK, I'd like to head down to Toronto with a Fiero group sometime this summer, maybe check out RSM, etc.. It'll have to be a time when we have more people than just Dave & I though..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000028||olympic||06-30-2000||10:42 PM||||BN Boomer,<BR>    Nope, R12 has been banned here as well.  You COULD still get your car recharged but I havn't seen one of those little cans of R12 in a long time.  I had my car refilled last fall and R12 was going for $60/lb then.   THe shop wasn't sure they could get anymore either.  I'm just going to buy a R134 conversion kit next time I need a recharge.<P>  BTW, I live in a rail road town and I know of the "evils" of which you speak.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000029||Sillhouette.com||06-30-2000||11:38 PM||||You cannot work in U.S. unless you have a work permit or the green card.  The green card will not be give to you unless the company you work for sponsors you and no company will sponsor a new employee.  I think it is harder for a Canadian to work in U.S than the other way around.  I currently work for a U.S. company and live in canada.  I'm quite lucky to work for U.S. dollars and live in Canada benefits.  It's the best of both worlds.  I don't know why you would want to work in Canada the dollar is pathetic and it will kill you on the exhancge.<P>R12 going rate is 600 dollars (Canadian) a pound.<P>Drop me a line when you all plan on visiting RSM so that I make sure they are there.  During the summer months we race a lot with various clubs and there are days when we are not at the shop.  <P>Later||||reg||1
